{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — THE CIRCLE, request access.

  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ⚠️  TERMINOLOGY CONFLICT — RAISED WITH ALOHA, BUILT ON HER WRITTEN
      INSTRUCTION OF 4 SEPTEMBER 2026.

      CLAUDE.md records Framework v3, which is the top of the source-of-truth
      hierarchy and says of The Circle:

          "Invitation-only group of founding friends.
           No public form. No application route."

      Aloha's email asks for the opposite — a public page carrying a Circle
      access form. Her instruction is second in the hierarchy, below
      Christina's Framework v3, so this is a conflict the build cannot resolve
      on its own and Christina has to settle it.

      It is built because Aloha asked for it in writing and because it is on an
      unpublished development theme where nothing is public. It is built to be
      switched off in one click: `show_form` off leaves the page, the wording
      and the layout intact and removes the application route entirely. No
      other section depends on it.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  --- WHAT REACHES THE CRM ------------------------------------------------
  Aloha: "Anyone submitting the Circle access form should be added to the
  CRM/Register with the tag 'Circle: Requested Access.' Joining The Register
  alone should not automatically give someone access to The Circle."

  This uses Shopify's own customer form, the same one The Register uses, so a
  submission creates a real customer record rather than an email someone has to
  re-key. `contact[tags]` is Shopify's supported way to tag that record from the
  storefront — the pattern is already in this theme in five places, including
  ha-register.liquid.

  The two directions Aloha asked to keep separate are kept separate BY THE TAG,
  which is the only thing that can keep them separate in one customer list:

      The Register  ->  tag  "register"                (ha-register.liquid)
      The Circle    ->  tag  "Circle: Requested Access"  (here)

  A Register member is not tagged for the Circle and never becomes one by
  joining. A Circle applicant IS added to the Register — which is what Aloha
  asked for — and carries the extra tag that marks the request. Nothing in the
  theme grants Circle access; the tag records that access was requested, and a
  human decides. That is the whole mechanism, and it is deliberately not
  automatic.

  Stated interests are appended as their own tags, from the fixed list of
  checkboxes below, so they arrive as CRM segments rather than as prose. The
  vocabulary is controlled — a visitor cannot invent a tag — which is what keeps
  the customer list clean. See assets/ha-circle-request.js.

  --- 14 SEPTEMBER: THE FORM NOW POSTS TO KLAVIYO ---------------------------
  assets/ha-klaviyo-form.js sends this markup to Klaviyo's client subscription
  endpoint, into the `Circle Requests` list — its own list, separate from The
  Register, per the completion plan. Interests go with it as a `circle_interests`
  property, and the city and note fields are finally real: they travel as
  profile properties, which Shopify's customer form could never carry.

  Everything above about Shopify tags still holds for the NO-JS path only. With
  the script running, Shopify is not posted to.

  The Circle constraint is unchanged: landing on `Circle Requests` records that
  access was requested. Nothing here, and no flow, may read as acceptance.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign base_tag = section.settings.contact_tag | default: 'Circle: Requested Access'
-%}

<section
  id="{{ section.settings.anchor | default: 'request-access' }}"
  class="ha-section ha-crequest{% unless section.settings.field == 'page' or section.settings.field == blank %} ha-section--field-{{ section.settings.field }}{% endunless %}"
>
  <div class="ha-crequest__grid">

    {%- comment -%}
      The image is the full-bleed half of the composition, so it sits outside
      .ha-wrap and reserves its proportion like every other Hartwick figure.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ha-crequest__media">
      {%- render 'ha-figure',
        image: section.settings.image,
        label: section.settings.image_label,
        class: 'ha-crequest__figure',
        sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw',
        alt: section.settings.image_alt
      -%}
    </div>

    <div class="ha-crequest__panel">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="ha-eyebrow ha-record">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="ha-display ha-narrate ha-crequest__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <div class="ha-body ha-narrate ha-crequest__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_form -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          An app form — Klaviyo's — drops in here, same idiom as `ha-register`.
          This is a different switch from `show_form` above and the two must not
          be confused: `show_form` off removes the application route altogether,
          which is the Framework v3 answer. `show_native_form` only decides who
          carries the form when there is one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- case block.type -%}
            {%- when '@app' -%}
              {% render block %}
          {%- endcase -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_native_form -%}
        {%- form 'customer',
          class: 'ha-crequest__form',
          id: 'CircleRequest',
          novalidate: 'novalidate',
          data-nocaptcha: 'true',
          data-ha-klaviyo: '',
          data-company-id: settings.ha_klaviyo_company_id,
          data-list-id: settings.ha_klaviyo_circle_list,
          data-source: section.settings.register_source,
          data-msg-invalid: section.settings.msg_invalid,
          data-msg-consent: section.settings.msg_consent,
          data-msg-submitting: section.settings.msg_submitting,
          data-msg-success: section.settings.success_text,
          data-msg-error: section.settings.msg_error
        -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            The tag that does the work. JS rewrites this value to append the
            checked interests; with JS off it still submits exactly as written,
            so the requirement Aloha stated — the record carries
            "Circle: Requested Access" — is never dependent on a script.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="contact[tags]"
            value="{{ base_tag | escape }}"
            data-circle-base-tag="{{ base_tag | escape }}"
          >

          {%- comment -%} Live region for the script's states; Shopify's own two below are the no-JS path. {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="ha-crequest__note ha-record" data-ha-form-status tabindex="-1" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>

          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
            <p class="ha-crequest__note ha-crequest__note--ok ha-record" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{ section.settings.success_text | default: 'Thank you. Your request has been received.' }}
            </p>
          {%- elsif form.errors -%}
            <p class="ha-crequest__note ha-crequest__note--error ha-record" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="ha-crequest__pair">
            <div class="ha-crequest__field">
              <label class="ha-crequest__label ha-record" for="CircleFirst">{{ section.settings.label_first }}</label>
              <input class="ha-crequest__input ha-narrate" id="CircleFirst" type="text" name="contact[first_name]" autocomplete="given-name" value="{{ form.first_name }}">
            </div>
            <div class="ha-crequest__field">
              <label class="ha-crequest__label ha-record" for="CircleLast">{{ section.settings.label_last }}</label>
              <input class="ha-crequest__input ha-narrate" id="CircleLast" type="text" name="contact[last_name]" autocomplete="family-name" value="{{ form.last_name }}">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ha-crequest__field">
            <label class="ha-crequest__label ha-record" for="CircleEmail">{{ section.settings.label_email }}</label>
            <input
              class="ha-crequest__input ha-narrate"
              id="CircleEmail"
              type="email"
              name="contact[email]"
              autocomplete="email"
              autocorrect="off"
              autocapitalize="off"
              value="{{ form.email }}"
              aria-required="true"
              required
            >
          </div>

          {%- if section.settings.show_extra_fields -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Real since 14 September: `data-klaviyo-prop` is the property name
              the script writes on the profile. Shopify's form still drops the
              field on the no-JS path, which is why the switch stays.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="ha-crequest__field">
              <label class="ha-crequest__label ha-record" for="CircleCity">{{ section.settings.label_city }}</label>
              <input class="ha-crequest__input ha-narrate" id="CircleCity" type="text" name="contact[city_country]" autocomplete="address-level2" data-klaviyo-prop="city_country">
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- assign interest_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'interest' -%}
          {%- if interest_blocks.size > 0 -%}
            <fieldset class="ha-crequest__field ha-crequest__interests">
              <legend class="ha-crequest__label ha-record">{{ section.settings.label_interests }}</legend>
              <div class="ha-crequest__checks">
                {%- for block in interest_blocks -%}
                  <label class="ha-crequest__check ha-narrate" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Not a form field in its own right: the value is folded
                      into contact[tags] on submit, because Shopify would drop a
                      name it does not recognise. `data-circle-interest` is what
                      the script reads.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <input
                      type="checkbox"
                      data-circle-interest="{{ block.settings.tag | default: block.settings.label | escape }}"
                    >
                    <span>{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                  </label>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </fieldset>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.show_extra_fields -%}
            <div class="ha-crequest__field">
              <label class="ha-crequest__label ha-record" for="CircleNote">{{ section.settings.label_note }}</label>
              <textarea class="ha-crequest__input ha-crequest__textarea ha-narrate" id="CircleNote" name="contact[note]" rows="3" data-klaviyo-prop="circle_note"></textarea>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.consent_text != blank -%}
            <label class="ha-crequest__check ha-crequest__consent ha-narrate">
              <input type="checkbox" data-ha-consent required aria-required="true">
              <span>{{ section.settings.consent_text }}</span>
            </label>
          {%- endif -%}

          <button class="ha-crequest__submit ha-identify" type="submit">
            {{ section.settings.submit_text }}
          </button>
        {%- endform -%}

        <script src="{{ 'ha-circle-request.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
        <script src="{{ 'ha-klaviyo-form.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The switch that honours Framework v3. With the form off the section is
          still a section — heading, copy, picture — and simply does not offer
          an application route.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if section.settings.closed_text != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-crequest__closed ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.closed_text }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Circle request",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "max_blocks": 8,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "select", "id": "field", "label": "Field colour", "default": "page", "options": [
      { "value": "page", "label": "Page ground" },
      { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
      { "value": "peat", "label": "Peat (dark)" },
      { "value": "clay", "label": "Clay" },
      { "value": "slate", "label": "Slate (dark)" }
    ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Anchor id", "default": "request-access", "info": "Links elsewhere on the page point at #this." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Request access" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Tell us what you would like to follow." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Picture" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Alt text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_label", "label": "Placeholder label", "default": "01 / Portrait" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "The form",
      "info": "⚠ Framework v3 records The Circle as invitation-only, with no public form and no application route. This form exists on Aloha's written instruction of 4 September 2026 and the conflict is with Christina to settle. Switching it off removes the application route and leaves everything else on the page intact."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_form", "label": "Show the access form", "default": true },
    {
      "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_native_form", "label": "Show the form", "default": true,
      "info": "This form posts to Klaviyo. Switch off only if a Klaviyo app block is carrying the form instead — never both. This is not the Framework v3 switch — that is 'Show the access form' above."
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "register_source", "label": "Klaviyo source", "default": "circle_page",
      "info": "Recorded on the profile as register_source."
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "contact_tag", "label": "CRM tag", "default": "Circle: Requested Access",
      "info": "Applied to the customer record created by every submission. The Register uses its own separate tag, so joining one never joins the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_extra_fields", "label": "Ask for city and a note", "default": true,
      "info": "Stored on the Klaviyo profile as city_country and circle_note. Only the no-JS fallback (Shopify's own form) drops them."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_first", "label": "First name label", "default": "First name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_last", "label": "Last name label", "default": "Last name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_email", "label": "Email label", "default": "Email address" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_city", "label": "City label", "default": "City / country" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_interests", "label": "Interests label", "default": "I would like to hear about" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_note", "label": "Note label", "default": "A note, if you would like to add one" },
    {
      "type": "richtext", "id": "consent_text", "label": "Consent line",
      "default": "<p>[PLACEHOLDER — wording from Christina] Yes, you may contact me about this request. I can withdraw at any time.</p>",
      "info": "Required to submit and never pre-ticked. The wording is a legal matter under CASL — Aloha to confirm with Christina."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "submit_text", "label": "Submit button", "default": "Send request" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Messages" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_text", "label": "Success message", "default": "Thank you. Your request has been received — a confirmation is on its way to your inbox.", "info": "Must not read as acceptance into The Circle. The list is double opt-in, so it also has to send them to their inbox." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_invalid", "label": "Invalid email", "default": "Please enter a valid email address." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_consent", "label": "Consent not ticked", "default": "Please tick the box to send your request." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_submitting", "label": "While sending", "default": "One moment…" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "msg_error", "label": "Service error", "default": "That did not go through. Please try again, or write to contact@hartwickatelier.com." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "closed_text", "label": "Text shown when the form is off", "info": "Used instead of the form when the access form is switched off." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Provisional content" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_placeholder_note", "label": "Show placeholder notice", "default": true }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@app" },
    {
      "type": "interest",
      "name": "Interest",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "tag", "label": "CRM tag", "info": "Added to the customer record when ticked. Defaults to the label." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Hartwick — Circle request" }]
}
{% endschema %}
